52	Wellness Academy_chunk_0013	l., 2010) compared to non-impact \nactivities. Active participation in soccer or football \npositively affects whole body bone mineral density \nin children and adolescents (Lozano-Berges et al., \n2018).\n\nPhysical activity contributes to bone health by \nincreasing the width and mineral content of bones in \ngirls and adolescent females, mainly when initiated \nbefore puberty (Borer, 2005). The greatest increases \nin bone mass occurs between the age of 12-15 years \nin girls compared to 14-17 years in boys (Davies et \nal., 2005). Almost half of the adult bone mass is \naccumulated during the growth spurt in adolescence \n(Parfitt, 1994).	[0.059032608,0.039066277,-0.0785082,0.029524622,-0.04353065,-0.0331928,-0.019718258,0.03136681,0.01690026,-0.010809362,0.007145217,0.039872482,-0.057008006,-0.015643472,0.01627401,-0.01827967,-0.013497719,-0.026478862,-0.0013182057,0.01177839,-0.011346343,0.00034044925,0.0006115878,0.007650423,0.04056064,0.034141194,0.0125568705,0.001992398,0.017699579,0.06207641,0.0037696718,0.013534389,0.0700237,-0.030999629,0.005013233,-0.013675299,-0.0005426726,-0.07402139,-0.03192956,0.016892202,-0.0031090705,-0.039718427,0.012633541,0.019078404,-0.020408662,-0.041358918,-0.014588898,-0.01678802,-0.015168827,-0.07875411,-0.03233839,-0.01707896,0.042163953,-0.028869655,0.01909469,0.03952507,0.02950444,0.013537849,-0.046398547,-0.02698747,0.004295295,0.030904297,-0.023335213,-0.028094389,-0.033506665,0.022504881,0.038986932,-0.011300358,-0.01681031,-0.057577007,0.018248446,0.03169667,0.021403415,-0.03219532,-0.034543715,0.002098852,0.0059496188,0.02189655,0.011117668,0.0021531396,-0.0043444782,-0.025032401,-0.033765845,-0.012847403,-0.054672696,-0.008122335,0.011349877,0.016183062,0.0033302808,-0.013112911,0.009029714,-0.038374525,0.01580008,-0.042758327,0.015535951,0.034944054,-0.023000991,-0.033977095,0.030026356,-0.0092733465,0.032761738,0.026067156,0.009669702,-0.057178564,0.023726387,0.010114793,0.02175569