55	Wellness Academy_chunk_0016	chronic illnesses, \nsuch as cardiovascular diseases and diabetes, \nand infections such as pneumonia and influenzas \n(Eggersdorfer et al., 2018). Addressing nutrient deficiency is important in old age.\n\nA study that evaluated nutrient intake adequacy of \nmore than 4,000 US adults aged 51 years and older, \nfound that a large proportion of them do not consume \nrequired amounts of many essential nutrients from \nfoods alone (Sebastian et al., 2007). The same study \ndiscovered that while supplements helped meet the \nrecommended nutrient intake to some degree, only  \nhalf of the study group used them on a daily basis. During old age, bone breakdown outpaces bone \nformation. This reduction in bone density predisposes \none to osteoporosis and overall frailty. The rate of bone \nloss is higher in aging women compared to men (Borer, \n2005) due to changes in post-menopausal reproductive \nhormones. High intensity resistance exercises have \nshown improvement in bone mineral density in healthy \nelderly subjects (Rhodes et al., 2000; Vincent and \nBraith, 2002). Calcium supplementation along with \nexercise has been found effective in slowing bone \nloss in post-menopausal women (Prince et al., 1991). Higher body weight is linked to lower fracture risk in old \nage due to greater bone mineral density (Yang et al., \n2013). Higher peak bone mass achieved during early \nadult life reduces the risk of osteoporosis later in life \n(Demontiero et al., 2012).	[0.041012738,0.027696198,-0.0820475,0.0061614085,-0.04370034,-0.03444687,0.014382151,0.03253001,-0.0161758,0.0093232915,-0.010311152,-0.016889274,-0.045918807,0.027196256,0.023508538,-0.031155374,-0.014821027,-0.004616116,-0.06467627,0.025010552,-0.007702283,0.00086340983,0.04928801,0.008392495,0.003003885,0.02831539,-0.0010654483,-0.013184666,0.023153413,0.029390136,-0.010481894,-0.019055562,0.04268054,-0.008274482,-0.011425802,0.0048496844,0.011840427,-0.054851104,-0.034233075,0.053