40	Wellness Academy_chunk_0001	By Silvi Siddhu,  \nDirector, Nutraceuticals \nUnivar Solutions\nOptimizing Health Throughout the Life Cycle: \nThe Need for Active Nutrition\n\n2\nWellness Academy | The Need for Active Nutrition\nABSTRACT\nA balanced diet and regular physical activity are the \ntwo major lifestyle factors known to influence and \nimprove various aspects of health. The cooperative \naction of nutrition and exercise at the molecular \nlevel affects overall health and well-being and has \na critical role in influencing cognitive abilities across \nthe lifespan. Together they help in the growth and \nmaintenance of muscle mass, bone mineral density \nand influence hippocampal volume that is linked to \nlearning, memory and overall cognitive health. There \nis robust evidence that stipulates the importance of \nearly years in physical, cognitive and socioemotional \ndevelopment that continues throughout life. Regular \nphysical exercise helps improve memory and acts as an \nantidepressant and analgesic via various mechanisms. Physical activity’s positive effect on attenuation of \nneurodegenerative disorders makes it an effective non-\npharmacological intervention in managing disorders \nsuch as Alzheimer’s, Parkinson’s and dementia. Sleep, \nA healthy lifestyle is \nimportant to allow \nhealthy aging. \nin addition to diet and exercise plays a mediating \nrole in mental health. A healthy lifestyle is important \nto allow healthy aging. In this perspective, the role \nof active nutrition (converging diet, physical activity \nand supplementation) across all the stages in life \nis discussed. Implementation of better educational \nresources will help everyone make informed decisions \nabout appropriate diet, exercise and nutritional \nsupplements for their health needs. Encouraging a \nhealthier, more active lifestyle early in life will have the \npotential to reduce chronic disease risk later in life and \npromote healthy aging. INTRODUCTION\nGood health and well-being are fundamental human \nrights. Health is not limited to just physiological well-\nbeing but includes all aspects of human health – \nphysical, mental, emotional and social. Aging affects \nevery aspect of human life. Average life expectancy  \nhas continuously improved over the last century \nglobally, however, an increase in health span will \nrequire prolonging well-being and delaying aging  \nrather than averting death. In 2019, the average global \nlife expectancy was 73.4 years (WHO, 2022c). Delayed \naging has the potential to extend healthy years of life \nand postpone health deterioration over the life cycle \n(Goldman et al., 2013). In 2013, while the life expectancy \nin America was 77 years, the ‘health life expectancy’ \nwas at an estimated 67 years (NASEM, 2016). The human body constantly progresses throughout  \nits life cycle. The role of nutrition and physical activity \nin shaping various elements of human health, including \nhealthy aging, is enormous and continually explored. There is an overwhelming amount evidence on the \ninfluence of diet and physical activity on both physical \nand cognitive health. Physical activity is defined as  \nany bodily movement produced by skeletal muscles \nthat results in energy expenditure, and exercise is a \nsubset of physical activity (Caspersen et al., 1985;  \nDi Liegro et al., 2019). Healthy nutrition and physical activity are two \nmain lifestyle factors strongly linked to improved \nbody composition, overall physical performance, \nmusculoskeletal health, cognitive health and metabolic \nhealth across the lifespan (Koehler and Drenowatz, \n2019). There are a number of factors that influence \nphysical and mental health at each life stage.	[0.027151711,0.0036131174,-0.04437411,-0.025091229,-0.032592673,-0.013721239,-0.015776943,-0.012018799,-0.00025762626,-0.019185942,0.0075390777,-0.020097537,-0.08902781,-0.0005489072,-0.0064189523,-0.011279211,-0.0014752303,-0.019095546,-0.04019514,0.016734