107	The Peter Attia Drive - AMA #72: Fasting: benefits for body composition and disease prevention, potential risks, and Peter's updated practical framework_chunk_0002	I think politics is an area where it's very difficult to change your mind and maintain credibility.\n\nIt seems that the harder you dig in on your position, the more credible you seem. So again to be clear, I think this should be viewed as a feature, not a bug in life, but "it should especially be viewed as a feature in the field of science and medicine where there's no such thing as absolute certainty, so people have heard me say this before, but everything in science is probabilistic, and there are certain things where the probability is so high that it is effectively a certainty, so if I were to drop a bowling ball while standing on planet earth, I can say with essentially near certainty that it will accelerate towards the ground at 9ine." 8 meters per second squared, but we shouldn't lose sight of the fact that there's a actually a probability function that is telling us that. I've been as you not, I think or alluded to, I've had people get angry at me on social media when I've posted you, a changing position on something, most notably or most recently discussions around GLP-1 agonis, and so I think on a recent post I quoted Johnard Keys, when he was asked why he changed his mind on something, and he responded, and I love this, when the facts change, I change my mind, what? do you do, sir? I love that quote. I think the best way I could say it is the way I try to think on every topic is being in a constant state of evolution, and I'm not wed to being right, I'm wed to knowing what is right, and I think that's probably the single most important piece of my mental scaffolding, that if someone asked me, hey, Peter, what's a good way to orient myself to information? I would say, that is it. I'm not. suggesting that that's unique to me, i think a lot of people do that, but that's what i would recommend to people is orient yourself towards knowing what is right and less around being right, then you'll constantly find yourself going in the right direction. thank you for that level set. all right, getting started, fasting. i think it'd be helpful just to define the different terms around fasting, when you've talked about nutrition in the past, and you've talked about the need to make sure you watch how many calories you eat, you've talked about dr, tr, cr framework, so do you just want to spend a minute defining these terms as we'll talk about them today? so when we mention different things, people understand what specifically we're talking about? yeah, so taking a step way back, people criticize me for not being as dogmatic as maybe I once was, or as others are when it comes to nutrition, but the truth of the matter is, all the available evidence basically says the following: you need to be in energy balance, so too much and too little is bad, you need... adequate amounts of protein, that seems to be the one constant, you have to be able to maintain lean mass, but the actual amount of carbohydrates and fats, provided your an energy balance doesn't seem to matter that much. you obviously need to have sufficient amount of micronutrients and you need to avoid toxins, and once you sort of get through that, it's an open canvas as to what you want to do. now for most of us, i certainly include myself in this position, maintaining energy balance requires some effort. what that means is i can't just eat whatever I want, whenever I want, in whatever quantity I want. If I did that, I would be out of energy balance, I would be metabolically unhealthy, and I would deal with all the sequele of that.	[-0.022441706,0.013229757,-0.033712663,0.028589264,-0.02798704,-0.07828332,-0.021414604,-0.010038558,-0.00012730224,-0.019596364,-0.023557456,-0.008724938,-0.031755675,0.01824977,0.016999213,-0.010473571,-0.0046844725,0.0069725537,0.010940954,-0.019473284,-0.014426528,-0.028978162,0